    {
      "id": "2114753529034498321",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-10-26T16:18:26.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-27 00:18:26",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "Michael Dell calls Elon Musk the \"most demanding customer there is,\" and says Musk rewarded Dell with more business after the Colossus build\n\nDELL: “So it shouldn’t be too surprising that we’re also number one in AI infrastructure.”\n\nMIMS: “Dell did half of the servers in the Colossus One AI supercomputer for SpaceX. And you did it really fast, right? I think that was a record fast build. It was like six weeks or something.”\n\nDELL: “Elon is probably the most demanding customer. No, he’s definitely the most demanding customer there is.”\n\nMIMS: “Yeah? Was there a bonus involved? Get this done in six weeks and…”\n\nDELL: “I don’t know that there was a bonus involved, but they have rewarded us with additional business because we’ve done a great job. And that’s pretty much the pattern.”",
      "quote": {
        "author": "firesidealpha",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2066254089756061697/MGnZGljz_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-25 12:27:46",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-10-25T04:27:46.000Z",
        "id": "2114212298625827094",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2114212103431352320/img/wSWfYo6KxggxpiFg.jpg"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "duration": 56.473,
            "height": 1080,
            "thumbnail_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2114212103431352320/img/wSWfYo6KxggxpiFg.jpg",
            "type": "video",
            "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2114212103431352320/vid/avc1/1920x1080/8-RICf0_W6S6ljNl.mp4?tag=29",
            "width": 1920
          }
        ],
        "name": "Fireside Alpha",
        "text": "Elon Musk explains how to build AI satellites on the moon from lunar silicon and aluminum, and says 500 to 1,000 terawatts a year cannot be launched from Earth\n\n“Well, the lunar soil is 20% silicon or something like that. So you can mine the silicon on the moon, refine it, and create the solar cells and the radiators on the moon. So get the radiators out of aluminum. So there’s plenty of silicon and aluminum on the moon to make the cells and the radiators. The chips you could send from Earth because they’re pretty light. But maybe at some point you make them on the moon, too.\"\n\n\"Like I said, it does seem like a sort of a video game situation where it’s difficult but not impossible to get to the next level. I don’t see any way that you could do 500 to 1,000 terawatts per year launched from Earth.”",
        "url": "https://x.com/firesidealpha/status/2114212298625827094",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
